.\"
.\" SYNC(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH SYNC 2 "2026-02-28" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
sync \- commit filesystem caches to disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.B void sync(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sync ()
causes all pending modifications to filesystem metadata and cached
file data to be written to the underlying filesystems.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR sync ()
always succeeds.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 36
Arguments:      none
.fi
.SS Behavior
On Substrate
.BR sync ()
is synchronous: it writes every file system's deferred metadata and
every dirty buffer to its device, then asks each block device to flush
its volatile write cache, and returns only when all of that is done.
POSIX allows
.BR sync ()
to return before the writes complete; programs that need a guarantee
for particular files should still use
.BR fsync (2),
which on Substrate does the same work.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fsync (2),
.BR mount (2),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008.
